# Participant data must never be committed.
#
# Video is the obvious case, but a landmark CSV is a face: 478 points
# per frame is enough to reconstruct one, and the mask renders are
# identifiable to anyone who knows the person. The plot tree is
# aggregated but its filenames and axis labels carry session dates.
#
# If you fork this for your own study, run `git status` before your
# first push, and remember that absolute paths saved in settings can
# themselves identify a study or a participant.

# recordings
*.mp4
*.mov
*.MP4
*.MOV
*.avi
*.mkv
*.webm

# renders facekit produces
*_landmarks.mp4
*_only_mask.mp4
*_mesh.mp4

# landmark and metric tables
*.csv
*.tsv
face_landmarks.csv
all_landmarks.csv
all_frame_metrics.csv

# figures
*.pdf
plots/
best_quartile/

# saved settings, presets and review progress
.facekit/
settings.json
presets/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# editors and platforms
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# the documentation screenshots are the deliberate exception
!docs/*.png
